cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ColdDDI in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ColdDDI: Evaluating Knowledge Utilization in Cold-Start Drug-Drug Interaction Prediction"
abstract: >-
  ColdDDI is a benchmark for evaluating drug-drug interaction prediction methods
  under cold-start settings, comprising 1,900 drugs and 565,731 positive pairs
  from DrugBank 5.1.13. Each interaction is stratified by pharmacological
  mechanism (PK/PD) and by whether shared mediating entities are present in the
  knowledge graph (Type A/B). The benchmark evaluates 8 conventional baselines
  and 13 LLMs across 5 prompt patterns, with diagnostic metrics quantifying
  knowledge utilization.
